// Title: Use Icacls to Hide File to Everyone
// Sigma ID: 4ae81040-fc1c-4249-bfa3-938d260214d9
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-07-18 | Modified: 2024-04-29
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.001
// Description: Detect use of icacls to deny access for everyone in Users folder sometimes used to hide
//   malicious files
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/1df999e6-1cb8-45e3-8b61-499d1b7d5a9b/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_icacls_deny.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "iCACLS.EXE" or FolderPath endswith "\\icacls.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/deny" and ProcessCommandLine contains "S-1-1-0:")
